 =\sum_{e=uv}w_eP_{uv}
 =Q_{\mathrm{EPR}}.
\]
The second equality follows by multiplying the displayed Pauli matrices.
Therefore
\[
 \lambda_{\max}(Q_{\mathrm{cut}})=\lambda_{\max}(Q_{\mathrm{EPR}}),
 \qquad Z_\beta(Q_{\mathrm{cut}})=Z_\beta(Q_{\mathrm{EPR}}).
\]
The EPR algorithms prove both remaining claims.
